From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:54:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tls/tests/connection.c: Ignore client close error in
 missing-private-key test with openssl

With TLS 1.3 the server rejects the client certificate after the client
has finished its side of the handshake, so the certificate-required alert
is reported again when the client closes the connection. The
client-auth-failure test already ignores the close error for this
reason, and the missing-private-key test does the same for the openssl
backend on Windows. On Linux (openssl 4.0, musl) it fails every time too:

GLib-Net:ERROR:../sources/glib-networking-2.80.1/tls/tests/connection.c:545:on_client_connection_close_finish: assertion failed (error == NULL): Server required TLS certificate (g-tls-error-quark, 5)
not ok /tls/openssl/connection/client-auth-fail-missing-client-private-key

Ignore the close error for the openssl backend on all platforms. The
test still checks the read and server errors.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
---
 tls/tests/connection.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tls/tests/connection.c b/tls/tests/connection.c
index ac70a70..c58b8fc 100644
--- a/tls/tests/connection.c
+++ b/tls/tests/connection.c
@@ -1685,7 +1685,7 @@ test_client_auth_fail_missing_client_private_key (TestConnection *test,
   /* All validation in this test */
   g_tls_client_connection_set_validation_flags (G_TLS_CLIENT_CONNECTION (test->client_connection),
                                                 G_TLS_CERTIFICATE_VALIDATE_ALL);
-#if BACKEND_IS_OPENSSL && defined(G_OS_WIN32)
+#if BACKEND_IS_OPENSSL
   test->ignore_client_close_error = TRUE;
 #endif
 
@@ -1693,7 +1693,7 @@ test_client_auth_fail_missing_client_private_key (TestConnection *test,
   g_main_loop_run (test->loop);
   wait_until_server_finished (test);
 
-#if BACKEND_IS_OPENSSL && defined(G_OS_WIN32)
+#if BACKEND_IS_OPENSSL
   test->ignore_client_close_error = FALSE;
 #endif
 
